eai-ispatialgym is BUILD_ONLY (PROTOCOL §2.4): it is never pushed to a registry, and every host that runs iSpatialGym
tasks builds it locally.

Why: it is eai-behavior (the official stanfordvl/behavior:3.9.2 by digest + ffmpeg: NVIDIA Isaac Sim 5.1.0 and Omniverse
Kit, whose licences forbid redistribution) with iSpatialGym's BEHAVIOR-1K fork, NVlabs cuRobo v0.8.0 and iSpatialGym on
top; and iSpatialGym's repository is private, with no licence file.

Build (from the repository root; Docker with BuildKit):
  1. eai-behavior, as images/behavior/BUILD_ONLY says:
       docker build -t ghcr.io/mll-lab-nu/eai-behavior:$(cat images/behavior/VERSION) -f images/behavior/Dockerfile .
  2. a clean checkout of iSpatialGym at the pinned commit (needs read access to kmy17518/iSpatialGym):
       git clone -b ispatialgym-eval-release https://github.com/kmy17518/iSpatialGym.git /tmp/isg
       git -C /tmp/isg checkout 6c1ed2e7ead746129a7aa4648618f9f6063e1ec3
     The Dockerfile refuses any tree whose hash (every file but .git/, by path and content) is not ISG_TREE_SHA256.
  3. docker build --build-context ispatialgym=/tmp/isg \
       -t ghcr.io/mll-lab-nu/eai-ispatialgym:$(cat images/ispatialgym/VERSION) -f images/ispatialgym/Dockerfile .
The BEHAVIOR-1K fork (public) and cuRobo are fetched by commit during the build; constraints.txt fixes the versions of
everything the cuRobo install adds (a rebuild on 2026-10-14 gave the same `pip freeze`).

Licences the builder accepts: the NVIDIA Isaac Sim / Omniverse terms of the official image. BEHAVIOR-1K's code is MIT;
cuRobo is NVIDIA's (its licence ships with it). iSpatialGym: none stated (docs/benchmarks/ispatialgym.md, Known issues).

Data, needed to run (never in the image): the licensed BEHAVIOR Data Bundle, mounted read-only at run time from
$RCB_BEHAVIOR_DATA: omnigibson-robot-assets/ (3.8.2), behavior-1k-assets/ (3.9.0) and omnigibson.key, the same directory
BEHAVIOR-1K's tasks mount. The image itself holds iSpatialGym's small `ispatialgym-assets` dataset at /data.

GPU: an RTX-class NVIDIA GPU (Isaac Sim needs one even headless) and the NVIDIA container toolkit.
